  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "A lot of people assume a strong currency automatically means a strong economy. That is simply not true.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "flagStack",
          "country": "jp",
          "trend": "up",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Strong currency",
            "≠ strong economy."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A currency's value is really just a price, set by supply, demand, and above all, trust.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "globe",
          "kicker": "what it really is",
          "line": "It's a price",
          "sub": "supply, demand, and trust"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Take the US dollar. It is on one side of about eighty-eight percent of every currency trade on Earth.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "bigValue": 88,
          "bigSuffix": "%",
          "label": "of FX trades use the dollar",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "bill"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "narration": "The Bank for International Settlements measures trillions of dollars changing hands every single day.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "bis-fx",
          "kicker": "BIS · FX turnover"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "That dominance isn't about perfection, it is because the world trusts the dollar as its reserve.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-reserve",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · reserve currency"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Meanwhile, a big number on a banknote means nothing by itself. One Zimbabwean note once read a hundred trillion dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "big": "100T",
          "label": "Zimbabwe dollars — near worthless",
          "props": [
            "fire",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "narration": "Hyperinflation turned that enormous number into basically worthless paper.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-zim",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Zimbabwean dollar"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "So, strong number or strong trust, which would you actually rather hold?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
          "art": "globe",
          "line": "Which would you hold?",
          "sub": "Strong number, or strong trust?"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    }
  ]
}